{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>צב.</b> Like ובצבים ובפרדים — a species of cattle that draws wagons. Some say it has the sense of 'overly full,' from the root of ואת בטנך צבה בדרך רחוקה." "I have already explained in Sefer Moznayim: the mem of שנים עשר is joined and well-known, and the meaning is 'twelve,' with שנים עשר in construct to עשר as a shortening, just as שלש עשרה and similarly שלש אלה. And the word שני עשר comes with the mem dropped, by way of short form." "<b>על שני הנשאים.</b> Like לשני." "Scripture says וקרבנו, for it has already mentioned the offerer, and the vav has the force of saying 'and this is his offering.' And it says, for the second one, הקריב את קרבנו, for such is the way of Scripture — like ויאמר יצחק אל אברהם אביו ויאמר אבי, because the matter was prolonged; and similarly ויאמר המלך אחשורוש ויאמר לאסתר המלכה. And it does not mention הקריב for the rest of the princes, for it seized upon the short form. And similarly לגלגלותם in the census of Reuben and Simeon alone, and so many others."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:47.183029872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}